      "local_deviation": "The Cloud message-bus DLQ has no Local equivalent. Local retry and recovery remain owned by their specific sidecar outbox contracts rather than a fabricated global queue.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Desktop has a real global-admin Dead Letter Queue loader, App binding, strict DTO client, controller and complete native page. However workbenchCapabilityClient still wraps deadLetterQueueCapability with declared renderer provenance. Snapshot v4 closes that active declaration to renderer_capability_authority_unobserved, so the route cannot currently advertise or execute any Cloud DLQ action despite the implemented module. Local does not call Cloud APIs and retains the stable cloud_message_bus_dlq_not_applicable disposition."
    }
